. The division deployed a new mobile app store, called the Samsung Printing Apps Center, on AWS instead of using a traditional IT environment. By using AWS, the division was able to deploy its Printing Apps Center on time and has the scalability to handle spikes in download traffic.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Samsung_Customer-Reference_Logo.f1e446519aef479af34def92f78a700fca210e52.png","displayLocation":"Asia Pacific","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eSamsung Electronic Printing is a division of the Seoul-based conglomerate. The division deployed a new mobile app store, called the Samsung Printing Apps Center, on AWS instead of using a traditional IT environment. By using AWS, the division was able to deploy its Printing Apps Center on time and has the scalability to handle spikes in download traffic.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Electronics \u0026 Semiconductors","sortDate":"2015-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/samsung/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Samsung","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2015","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"AWS Case Study: Samsung"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#use-case#websites-apps","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#use-case","name":"Websites \u0026 Web Apps","description":"Websites \u0026 Web Apps","dateCreated":"2020-08-20T04:28:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:36:00+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#websites-apps","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Websites \u0026 Apps","description":"Websites \u0026 Apps","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:32:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-03-05T03:54:13+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","l